// #3180: the stories behind the delivery jobs of every mission board — who needs the goods and why, and what came of it
// once they were handed in (school club report: "more story with the jobs — why the deliveries, and who wants them").
// The board's roll stays exactly as it was (item, amount, reward); the server picks one story of the job's item ("need")
// and place by a stable hash of the job's id, so a job keeps its story across reloads. "place": settlement | station |
// base (the player's own base, run by a resident quartermaster) | ship (cargo orders radioed to the board in the player's
// own ship — nobody stands at it, so a ship story never names a giver). Every delivery item of the boards needs at least
// two stories at every place (BoardStoryTests). Texts: mission.board.<place>.<key>.title / .desc / .thanks in
// data/locales (English + German mandatory); {giver} is the board's quartermaster, no digits (the amounts vary per job).
// "brief" is an English hint for the AI wording only (the backend tells the same story in its own words) — never shown.
// Tone (docs/user/PARENTS.md): warm, a little sci-fi, kid-friendly — nobody is in danger, every delivery makes things better.
